==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|recal||obsolete}}
* {{sense|to call again}} {{alt|en|re-call}}

===Etymology===
From {{af|en|re-|call}}, probably modelled on {{ncog|la|revocāre}}, {{ncog|fr|rappeler}}, {{m+|en|withcall}}.

===Pronunciation===
; Verb
* {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈkɔːl/|a=RP}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-recall (verb).wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{enPR|rĭkôl'''′'''|rēkôl'''′'''|a=GA}}, {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈkɔl/|/ɹiˈkɔl/}}
** {{IPA|en|/ɹɪˈkɑl/|[ɹɪˈkʰɑɫ]|/ɹiˈkɑl/|[ɹiˈkʰɑɫ]|a=cot-caught}}
** {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɪkɔl/|a=sometimes in sense 8}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔːl|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|re|call}}

; Noun
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹiːkɔːl/|a=RP}}
* {{enPR|rē'''′'''kôl′|rēkôl'''′'''|rĭkôl'''′'''|a=GA}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈɹiˌkɔl/|/ɹiˈkɔl/|/ɹɪˈkɔl/}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹiˌkɑl/|/ɹiˈkɑl/|/ɹɪˈkɑl/|[ɹiˈkʰɑɫ]|a=cot-caught}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-recall.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːkɔːl|ɔːl|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|re|call}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[withdraw]], [[retract]] (one's [[words]] etc.); to [[revoke]] (an [[order]]). {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#: {{syn|en|withcall|Thesaurus:recant}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[call back]], [[bring back]]{{,}} or [[summon]] (someone) to a specific [[place]], [[station]], etc. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#: {{ux|en|He was '''recalled''' to service after his retirement.}}
#: {{ux|en|She was '''recalled''' to London for the trial.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|US politics}} To [[remove]] an [[elected]] [[official]] through a [[petition]] and [[direct]] [[vote]].
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|author=Nellie Bowles|title=Hurt by Lockdowns, California’s Small Businesses Push to Recall Governor|date=2021-02-19|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2021/02/19/business/newsom-coronavirus-california.html|passage=That stop-start-stop has created a groundswell of anger toward Mr. Newsom, a Democrat in the third year of his first term, that is increasingly fueling a movement to '''recall''' him from office in one of the bluest of blue states.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251018184221/https://www.nytimes.com/2021/02/19/business/newsom-coronavirus-california.html|archivedate=18 October 2025}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[bring back]] (someone) {{m|en|to}} or {{m|en|from}} a particular mental or physical state, activity etc. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To [[call back]] (a [[situation]], [[event]], etc.) to one's [[mind]]; to [[remember]]; to [[recollect]]. {{defdate|from 16th c.}}
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=2008-06-15|author=Vanessa Grigoriadis|title=Up in Smoke|url=http://www.nytimes.com/2008/06/15/books/review/Grigoriadis-t.html
|passage=He '''recalls''' that experience in a smooth, speedy story, “The Monster Mash,” but these days he’s not sure he liked it too much &mdash; the disembowelings, the coolers of brains, the stench of decomposing corpses (“the smell of job security,” as one pathologist puts it) terrify him.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250814153248/https://www.nytimes.com/2008/06/15/books/review/Grigoriadis-t.html|archivedate=14 August 2025}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=2011-10-15
|author=Phil McNulty
|title=Liverpool 1 - 1 Man Utd
|work=w:BBC Sport
|url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15225853.stm
|page=
|passage=Ferguson, perhaps '''recalling''' how United had been comprehensively outfought in the 3-1 defeat at Liverpool last season, opted for a side with a more pragmatic look with Phil Jones moved into a midfield role.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20120129073752/http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport2/hi/football/15225853.stm|archivedate=29 January 2012}}
#* {{RQ:NYT|date=26 October 2021|author=Scott Dochterman|title=Run game, turnovers and physicality: Why football clichés have been anything but in the Iowa – Wisconsin rivalry|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20251117164829/https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/2912529/2021/10/26/run-game-turnovers-and-physicality-why-football-cliches-have-been-anything-but-in-the-iowa-wisconsin-rivalry/|passage=“I remember what kind of game it was,” [[w:Brian Ferentz|{{quote-gloss|Brian}} Ferentz]] said, who was Iowa’s run-game coordinator in 2015. “It was not a shootout, if I '''recall''' correctly. I do '''recall''' correctly. We had to come up with a stop on the goal line; that ultimately is what won that football game in 2015.{{nb...}}”}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[hearken back]] to, [[evoke]]; to be [[reminiscent]] of.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1907|author=Ronald M. Burrows|title=The Discoveries In Crete|page=6|text="The twinkling of the dancers' feet" comes to us in the ''Odyssey'' as a memory from that palace of Alkinoos, whose wonders '''recall''' to us so much that we have found in Crete.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To [[call]] again; to call another [[time]]. {{defdate|from 17th c.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[request]] or [[order]] the [[return]] of (a faulty product). {{defdate|from 20th c.}}
#* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Ramishah Maruf|title=Popular eye ointments may not be sterile, recall warns|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/02/28/business/eye-ointments-sterile-recall-fda|date=2024-02-28|passage=On Feb. 26, the FDA posted a voluntary recall from Brassica Pharma, which is '''recalling''' several eye ointments with expiration dates ranging from February 2024 to September 2025.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250815113711/https://www.cnn.com/2024/02/28/business/eye-ointments-sterile-recall-fda|archivedate=15 August 2025}}

