===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The action or fact of calling someone or something back.
## Request of the return of a faulty [[product]].
##: {{ux|en|'''recall''' campaign}}
##* {{RQ:en:CNN|author=Ramishah Maruf|title=Popular eye ointments may not be sterile, recall warns|url=https://www.cnn.com/2024/02/28/business/eye-ointments-sterile-recall-fda|date=2024-02-28|passage=The '''recall''' said that no injuries related to the potentially unsterile facility have been reported.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250815113711/https://www.cnn.com/2024/02/28/business/eye-ointments-sterile-recall-fda|archivedate=15 August 2025}}
## {{lb|en|chiefly|US politics}} The right or procedure by which a public [[official]] may be removed from office before the end of their term of office, by a vote of the people to be taken on the filing of a [[petition]] signed by a required number or percentage of qualified voters.
##: {{ux|en|'''recall''' petition}}
##: {{ux|en|representative '''recall'''}}
## {{lb|en|US politics}} The right or procedure by which the decision of a court may be directly reversed or annulled by [[popular vote]], as was advocated, in 1912, in the platform of the {{w|Progressive Party (United States, 1912)|Progressive Party}} for certain cases involving the police power of the state.
# [[memory|Memory]]; the [[ability]] to [[remember]].
# {{lb|en|information retrieval|machine learning}} The fraction of (all) [[relevant]] [[material]] that is returned by a [[search]].
#: {{syn|en|sensitivity}}
#: {{ux|en|precision and '''recall'''}}

